In `tests/qa/testcase.py`, each test calls `_drive_value`, which sets `_ACCOUNT_ID = None`, builds a template whose first mapping entry is always `{"v": ["a", "b"]}`, and invokes `_ForEachValueFnFindInMap.value` with `[mapping_name, {"Ref": "AWS::AccountId"}, "v"]`. In `_language_extensions.py`, `_ForEachValueRef.value` cannot resolve `AWS::AccountId` when `_ACCOUNT_ID` is `None`, so `_ForEachValueFnFindInMap.value` takes the fallback path: it sets `t_map_2_value` from the third argument to `"v"`, initializes `max_length = -1`, and iterates the mapping entries in insertion order. On the first iteration, `v` is the first entry’s value `{"v": ["a", "b"]}`, so the condition checks `isinstance(v["v"], list)` which is `True`, and `len(v["v"])` which is `2`, while `max_length` is still `-1`.

